  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reverse Trade Mission - Healthcare Executive Leadership Training Program, through Meridian International Center</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA funding partially supported a 21-day training program for Chinese healthcare executives to strengthen their capacity and to introduce best practices in U.S. healthcare management and information technology (IT) solutions. The program was supported by members of USTDAs U.S.-China Healthcare Cooperation Program, which were responsible for developing the curriculum and itinerary, and Chinas Health Human Resources Development Center (HHRDC), which together agreed to provide nearly $300,000 to cover the full cost of tuition, as well as fund the cost of international airfare for some delegates. The training program was undertaken in coordination with HHRDC, Colombia Universitys Mailman School of Public Health, and the University of California San Diego Healthcare System.</narrative>
  </description>
